From 5e6a6fce2e7da28f435e39c8567dc773361d2304 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rodey Seijkens <me@rodey.nl>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:45:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(autodetect): scan every UEFI volume, key entries by
 volume and path

Enumerate EFI_SIMPLE_FILE_SYSTEM_PROTOCOL handles and scan \EFI on each
volume instead of only the image's own. A volume is identified by the GPT
partition GUID in the device path HD node, or by the device path bytes when
there is no HD node.

Add "volume <name> partuuid=<guid>" config lines and the @<name>: loader
prefix. Entries without the prefix keep their current meaning. Autodetect
skips a loader that an explicit entry already starts from the same volume
and path, and hides the image's own systemd-boot.

Volume-qualified loaders are read and loaded from the named volume's device
path. Every identity, path and skip comparison ignores case, because FAT
does, so \EFI\MICROSOFT\Boot\bootmgfw.efi and \EFI\MICROSOFT\BOOT\BOOTMGFW.EFI
dedupe to one entry.

The unit suite gains volume line parsing, @name: parsing, (volume, path)
dedupe and autodetect skip tests.
